## Test planned
Add `app/tests/test_bridge_overlap.py`. One disposable fixture root holds two queued and claimed Clerk jobs. They share `bridge`, `bridge/delivery`, `bridge/store`, and `bridge/provenance`. Their delivery ids, job files, links, and instruction inputs differ.

Both calls start together on a `threading.Barrier`. Both use the allowlisted `fixture-sleep` worker, whose own 30 second hold makes the overlap observable. The test waits, at most 25 seconds, until both `started.marker` files exist and neither `result.json` exists yet. That observation is not a retry of a failed run. Each job must then show its own collected artifact, one launch, and one Clerk return. The artifact hashes must differ. A later identical call for each job must be already-recorded, with no new launch, no new event, and no stored-byte change. An occupied third delivery id must refuse and keep its planted bytes. Shared parents must stay ordinary directories.

The existing `app/tests/test_clerk_seam.py` still covers same-job overlap. This test does not claim an exactly-once guarantee. No model, network, arbitrary command, or real store.

Disposable copy, then `python -B app/tests/test_bridge_overlap.py` and `python -B app/tests/test_clerk_seam.py`, once each, sequentially. A product failure stays in the first log. Product files are not edited to clear it.

